  "title": "Simultaneous EEG and fMRI signals during sleep from humans",
  "description": "This dataset comprises simultaneous EEG and fMRI recordings from 33 healthy human participants during sleep and wakefulness. The study includes resting-state sessions before and after a visual-motor adaptation task, followed by multiple sleep sessions with polysomnographic staging. The simultaneous acquisition of high-resolution BOLD imaging and 32-channel EEG enables investigation of the neural and autonomic correlates of sleep-wake transitions and arousal dynamics.",
  "methods_description": "EEG data were collected using a 32-channel MR-compatible EEG system (Brain Products, Munich, Germany) simultaneously with fMRI acquisition. Each scanning session included an anatomical scan, two 10-minute resting-state sessions (before and after a visual-motor adaptation task), and multiple 15-minute sleep sessions. Sleep stages were scored for 30-second epochs across all sessions. The R128 marker in EEG signals corresponds to BOLD fMRI volume triggers for synchronization.",
